# typesugar Branding

Consistent branding across CLI, docs, packages, and GitHub.

## Identity

- **Name:** typesugar (always lowercase)
- **Tagline:** Syntactic sugar for TypeScript with zero calories.
- **Sub-tagline:** Typeclasses, operator overloading, pattern matching and more through compile-time macros and zero-cost abstractions.
- **Logo:** Crystalline sugar cube, purple-to-pink gradient, four-pointed sparkles

## Emoji Convention

| Emoji | Use                                                                           |
| ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 🧊    | Primary brand mark — CLI headers, banners, log prefixes, package descriptions |
| ✨    | Success states — "compiled", "setup complete", "all checks passed"            |
| ✓/✗/⚠ | Status indicators in CLI output (pass/fail/warn)                              |

### CLI Output Examples

```
🧊 typesugar v0.1.0
🧊 Compiling 12 files...
✨ Successfully compiled 12 files.

🧊 typesugar doctor
✓ TypeScript installed
✗ ts-patch not active
✨ All checks passed!
```

### Package Descriptions

Prefix the `description` field in each package.json with 🧊:

```json
"description": "🧊 Syntactic sugar for TypeScript with zero calories"
```

## Colors

### Brand Palette (CSS/Docs)

| Token        | Hex       | Use                       |
| ------------ | --------- | ------------------------- |
| Purple       | `#8b5cf6` | Primary brand, light mode |
| Purple light | `#a78bfa` | Primary brand, dark mode  |
| Purple deep  | `#7c3aed` | Accents                   |
| Pink         | `#ec4899` | Gradient stop             |
| Orange       | `#f97316` | Gradient stop             |

### CLI Colors (ANSI)

| Color         | Use                    |
| ------------- | ---------------------- |
| Cyan (bright) | Headers, command names |
| Green         | Success, pass          |
| Red           | Error, fail            |
| Yellow        | Warning                |
| Blue          | Fix suggestions        |
| Dim           | Secondary text         |

## Old Names

The project was previously named `macrots`, `typemacro`, `ttfx`. When encountering `[typemacro]`, `@ttfx/*`, or similar in code/logs/comments, update to `typesugar` / `@typesugar/*`.
